%N A400502 Decimal expansion of alpha_P, the unique minimizer of Sum_{p prime} 1/(p*log(p)^alpha) for alpha > 0.
%C A400502 S(alpha) = Sum_{p prime} 1/(p*log(p)^alpha) is strictly convex on (0,oo), tends to +oo as alpha -> 0+ and as alpha -> oo, and has a unique minimizer alpha_P = 1.6049933417... (denoted k_0 in earlier work of the author).
%C A400502 Equivalently, alpha_P is the unique root of Sum_{p prime} -log(log(p))/(p*log(p)^alpha) = 0: the single positive term, from p = 2, balances the negative contribution of the primes p >= 3.
%C A400502 S(1) = A137245 (Erdős primitive constant), S(2) = A319231. The minimum value is S(alpha_P) = 1.483871117658339597073459031911...
%C A400502 The analogous minimizer over all integers n >= 2, alpha_N = 2.4881010104..., is A400503.
%H A400502 Ramón Moya, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23005107">The critical exponent alpha_P of the Alpha family over the primes</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%F A400502 alpha_P is the unique root for alpha > 0 of Integral_{t=0..oo} t^(alpha-1)*(log(t) - Psi(alpha))*P(1+t) dt = 0, where P is the prime zeta function and Psi is the digamma function.
%e A400502 1.604993341774987050101165673593006550387270116663326586926757...
%o A400502 (Python)
%o A400502 from mpmath import mp, mpf, quad, primezeta, log, gamma, digamma, findroot, inf
%o A400502 mp.dps = 40
%o A400502 def dS(alpha):
%o A400502     w = lambda t: t**(alpha - 1) * (log(t) - digamma(alpha))
%o A400502     reg = quad(
%o A400502         lambda t: w(t) * (primezeta(1 + t) + log(t)),
%o A400502         [0, mpf(1)/4, 1]
%o A400502     )
%o A400502     sing = -2/alpha**3 - digamma(alpha)/alpha**2
%o A400502     tail = quad(
%o A400502         lambda t: w(t) * primezeta(1 + t),
%o A400502         [1, 4, 16, 64, inf]
%o A400502     )
%o A400502     return (reg + sing + tail) / gamma(alpha)
%o A400502 print(findroot(dS, mpf("1.605")))
%Y A400502 Cf. A137245, A221711, A319231, A354954, A400503.
%K A400502 nonn,cons,new
%O A400502 1,2
%A A400502 _Ramon Moya_, Sep 27 2026
